{
  "_comment": "Phase 8 buildable-structure catalog (ROADMAP.md 'Building, Settlement Expansion & Fencing System'), grown from Phase 4 Stage 2's 2-entry proof-of-mechanic set to the 18-entry library. Loaded by scripts/building_db.gd, same shape/conventions as data/items.json + scripts/item_db.gd. New optional, backward-additive fields per entry: interaction (\"\" | \"storage\" | \"trading_post\" - replaces the old is_storage bool; storage_shed migrated to \"interaction\": \"storage\"), daily_yield ({item_id: count} added to player inventory once per in-game day via structures.gd's day-tick, generically - no per-building code), capacity_unlock ({bonus_key: amount} one-time bonuses summed via scripts/building_effects.gd's recompute_capacity_unlocks, recomputed in FULL every time rather than incrementally applied), and effect (a string key into scripts/building_effects.gd's EFFECTS registry of bespoke per-tick callables, or a key read directly by a later stage's own logic - Watchtower/Antenna Tower's effect strings aren't tick callables, they're read by Stage 3's settler-arrival roll). Barn/Coop additionally use animal_housing and animal_capacity; only these two house livestock, and builder.gd limits them to the farm zone. Fields: kind keys scripts/structures.gd's BUILDING_COLORS flat-color placeholder table; size is [w, h] in 16px cells; cost items are deliberately limited to wood/stone/scrap_metal because those are the only resources the player can actually gather in-game right now (axe on a tree yields 3 wood; pickaxe on ore yields 2 stone + 1 scrap_metal - see scripts/farm.gd) - cloth_scrap/bottle_caps/fertilizer exist in items.json but have no gather source yet, so costing them would make a structure unbuildable. Placement UX is unchanged Stage-1/Phase-4-Stage-2 single-cell builder.gd flow - fences/gates/Barn/Coop are catalog entries, no drag/linear placement mode exists.",
